---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../site';
import { href } from '../lib/paths';
---
<Base title="About" description="What Enterprise Blueprints is and how its content is made.">
  <div class="container container--narrow">
    <header class="page-header">
      <h1>About Enterprise Blueprints</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        An open reference library of public-sector missions, the capabilities they depend on, and
        vendor-neutral patterns that might realize them.
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>What it is</h2>
      <p>
        Each mission describes a type of public organization, such as U.S. federal Offices of Inspector
        General. Outcomes describe the results the mission seeks, with measures for telling how they're
        going. Capabilities describe what that kind of organization must be able to do to get those results.
        Implementation patterns describe reusable approaches to realizing those capabilities.
      </p>
      <p>
        Statements about law and official responsibilities cite primary sources, with the date each source
        was last reviewed.
      </p>

      <h2>Using the content</h2>
      <p>
        The site's content and code are released under the MIT License. Every item has a stable ID, so tools
        can refer to it. The <a href={href('sources/')}>sources page</a> lists every reference the library
        cites, and the source is on <a href={site.repositoryUrl}>GitHub</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
